s^1 &amp; \dfrac{\alpha(1 + \alpha) - 1}{1 + \alpha} &amp; 0 \\
s^0 &amp; 1 &amp; 
\end{array}\] For the system to be stable, all elements in the first column must be strictly positive <ol><li>\(1 + \alpha &gt; 0 \implies \alpha &gt; -1\)</li><li>\(\alpha^2 + \alpha - 1 &gt; 0\)</li></ol> Solving the quadratic boundary \(\alpha^2 + \alpha - 1 = 0\): \[\alpha = \frac{-1 \pm \sqrt{1 - 4(1)(-1)}}{2} = \frac{-1 \pm \sqrt{5}}{2}\] \[\alpha \approx 0.618 \quad \text{or} \quad \alpha \approx -1.618\] Intersecting with \(\alpha &gt; -1\), we chose -0.618 \[\boxed{0.618}\]

